{"name":"Arugula","hex":"#75ad5b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arugula","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish-flowered Mediterranean herb of the mustard family with flavoured leaves, often eaten in salads, that has a distinct, peppery flavor, of three species:\nEruca spp., especially Eruca sativa (syn. Eruca vesicaria subsp. sativa)\nDiplotaxis tenuifolia","Eruca spp., especially Eruca sativa (syn. Eruca vesicaria subsp. sativa)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arugula"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eruca sativa","blocks":[{"text":"Eruca sativa is an edible annual plant in the family Brassicaceae. Other common names include salad rocket, garden rocket, colewort, roquette, ruchetta, rucola, rucoli, and rugula."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Eruca_sativa_sl11.jpg/330px-Eruca_sativa_sl11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eruca_sativa"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Eruca_sativa_1_IP0206101.jpg/250px-Eruca_sativa_1_IP0206101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Eruca_sativa_1_IP0206101.jpg/500px-Eruca_sativa_1_IP0206101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Eruca_sativa_1_IP0206101.jpg/250px-Eruca_sativa_1_IP0206101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEruca_sativa_1_IP0206101.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Rocket_Salad%2C_Arugula%2C_Roquette%2C_Rucola%2C_Rugula_%28Eruca_vesicaria_subsp._sativa%29.jpg/500px-Rocket_Salad%2C_Arugula%2C_Roquette%2C_Rucola%2C_Rugula_%28Eruca_vesicaria_subsp._sativa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped